// The Bench devcontainer of the course repository (spine section 9.2; ARCHITECTURE.md section 11.1; W0-T05).
//
// It opens this repository in the Bench image with a PostgreSQL 18.6 service container beside it, and it is what a
// Codespaces prebuild builds. `statespace doctor` runs when the container is created and says whether the tools
// match their pins; green is the recorded run RUN-doctor-devcontainer.
//
// The lab template's devcontainer.json (W2) is this file with a compose file of its own, in which the Bench service
// names the published image by digest in place of `build` (name@sha256:<64 hex digits>, the digest CI printed when it
// pushed the image that bench/image/Dockerfile built) and sets STATESPACE_BENCH_IMAGE to the same reference, so that
// receipts carry the digest. LAB-1 needs no devcontainer: it runs with `uv run`, or in the tab (spine section 12,
// item 34).
//
// Lean's sandbox does not start in a default container, and `statespace doctor` reports that as `failed`. To opt in
// to the profile that starts it, which relaxes the container's confinement, replace the `dockerComposeFile` line
// below by
//     "dockerComposeFile": ["docker-compose.yml", "docker-compose.sandbox.yml"],
// after reading docker-compose.sandbox.yml. The options are in a compose file because this devcontainer is
// compose-based: its container's runtime options belong to the compose service.
//
// A Codespaces prebuild is set up in the repository's settings (Codespaces, Prebuilds), not in a file: choose the
// default branch, the trigger "on configuration change", and a machine type. It builds bench/image/Dockerfile through
// docker-compose.yml, so a codespace then starts from the finished image.
{
  "name": "statespace Bench",
  "dockerComposeFile": ["<sandbox>/statespace/.devcontainer/docker-compose.yml", "<sandbox>/statespace/.devcontainer/docker-compose.sandbox.yml"],
  "service": "bench",
  "workspaceFolder": "/workspaces/statespace",
  "remoteUser": "learner",
  "shutdownAction": "stopCompose",
  // Never fail the creation of a container on a red doctor: it prints what differs, and a failed command would put a
  // codespace into recovery mode.
  "postCreateCommand": "statespace doctor || true"
}
